														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1539229">
									

<p>So the plot grows humans or scary animals into monsters, but a puppy grows into a nice dog instead of, for example, some kind of wolf thing? And plants just grow normally, but faster? Seems inconsistent to me.</p>
<p>Containment should be updated to keep the soil behind a sealed door, with the chamber constantly disinfected. Super-diseases will grow otherwise. The fact that the soil was previously contained exposed in Detroit makes one wonder how this didn't happen already. And from there I have to question how the plot came to the Foundation's attention&#8230; kids growing marijuana shouldn't register. Authorities having to clear away a two-story-tall pot plant might. The link between the outside world and the Foundation's attention needs to be firmed up.</p>
<p>Also nit-picky, but there's no need to list both the area and volume of the soil. 14&#160;m<sup>3</sup> will make any area you want, depending on the depth and shape you choose.</p>

							</div>

								
